Development tooling is distributed under its respective open-source license. `pnpm licenses list --prod` reports only MIT, ISC, Apache-2.0 and Python-2.0 runtime dependency groups.

Charset and Unicode data
------------------------
- Unicode Character Database 17.0.0 Blocks.txt and Microsoft CP936/CP950 mapping snapshots:
  https://www.unicode.org/Public/17.0.0/ucd/Blocks.txt
  https://www.unicode.org/Public/MAPPINGS/VENDORS/MICSFT/WINDOWS/
  Unicode Terms of Use: https://www.unicode.org/terms_of_use.html
- General Standard Chinese Characters Table (2013), digitized snapshot from
  chenny/General-Chinese-Characters-Table-Pro@579687e (MIT), based on the official text.
- Modern Chinese common/general character tables (1988), preserved snapshot from
  quanh/chinese-char-dict@97b5d4f. These are legacy standard facts.
- Taiwan Ministry of Education Commonly/less-commonly Used Characters, digitized snapshot from
  cjkvi/cjkvi-tables@096c255. Standard fact data; UI identifies it as a community digitization.
- Hong Kong List of Graphemes of Commonly-used Chinese Characters, digitized package from
  leonsilicon/list-of-graphemes-of-commonly-used-chinese-characters@07f649a (MIT), based on the 2000 revised publication.
- HKSCS-2016 snapshot from data.gov.hk, TSV conversion from yawnoc/hkscs-2016@1c5900f.
  Hong Kong Government open data terms apply to the original dataset.
- Functional character lists are project-maintained factual code-point selections under MIT.

Full fixed revisions, counts and source paths are documented in tools/charset-sources/README.md and docs/DATA.md.

Frequency data
--------------
- SUBTLEX-CH-CHR: Cai, Q. & Brysbaert, M. (2010), Chinese character frequencies based on film subtitles.
- JSON distribution: subtlex-ch-chr 0.0.0 (MIT), https://github.com/leonsilicon/subtlex-ch-chr
- The traditional-Chinese profile is derived from the corpus above with OpenCC character mappings
  (STCharacters.txt, TWVariants.txt), BYVoid/OpenCC@178f05d, Apache License 2.0:
  https://github.com/BYVoid/OpenCC. The snapshot and its license are in tools/charset-sources/opencc/.

